1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,125
When a system has an experience, can it retain something from it and use it later?

2
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:10,995
DEE explores this possibility through its own computational architecture.

3
00:00:11,285 --> 00:00:15,150
To understand it, seeing an answer on a screen is not enough.

4
00:00:15,225 --> 00:00:21,855
We need to observe how information moves, interacts, and changes what happens
next.

5
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:25,750
This is DEE's computational universe.

6
00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:30,000
It consists of positions arranged in three dimensions.

7
00:00:30,075 --> 00:00:36,335
At each step, the same rule updates their records through interactions in space.

8
00:00:36,435 --> 00:00:44,295
Within this environment, we can build organizations that receive signals, retain
relationships, and produce responses.

9
00:00:44,615 --> 00:00:52,865
What matters is that processing takes place through the system's evolution: its history
helps shape what can happen next.

10
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:56,550
Let's look at an experiment performed by DEE's engine.

11
00:00:56,600 --> 00:01:02,445
During teaching, signals meet and leave relationships that can be used later.

12
00:01:02,585 --> 00:01:07,530
When a new query arrives, those relationships take part in transforming it.

13
00:01:07,735 --> 00:01:11,885
The path and what was learned work together to produce the response.

14
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:17,460
This example therefore shows how an earlier experience contributes to a new
processing event.

15
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:21,495
A new query now arrives, with an initial value of twenty.

16
00:01:21,545 --> 00:01:24,645
It encounters the first learned record.

17
00:01:24,695 --> 00:01:33,305
The interaction transforms it, and the output of that first encounter continues through
three-dimensional space until it meets a second relationship.

18
00:01:33,490 --> 00:01:36,265
The next interaction completes the sequence.

19
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:38,315
The system returns thirty.

20
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:45,760
In the visualization, we see both encounters, first at one point in space and then at
another, separated by time and trajectory.

21
00:01:45,835 --> 00:01:47,435
The number itself is simple.

22
00:01:47,510 --> 00:01:57,998
The technological advance lies in the mechanism: the relationships were acquired
earlier, their supports participated later, and a trajectory within the universe connected

23
00:01:57,998 --> 00:01:58,910
both transformations.

24
00:01:58,985 --> 00:02:03,260
Controls help establish the contribution of these encounters.

25
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:11,210
This allows us to investigate how an organization acquires a function and later uses it
through new interactions.

26
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:16,125
An experience can leave something that continues to influence later events.

27
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:23,350
In DEE, that memory resides in the relationships retained by the organization; for
example, between a signal and a response.

28
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:27,610
When another query arrives, what was learned can contribute again.

29
00:02:27,685 --> 00:02:33,895
This is functional memory: retaining an experience so that it can be used later.

30
00:02:34,983 --> 00:02:36,808
And what has been learned can change.

31
00:02:36,903 --> 00:02:41,253
Here we see the same signal before and after a new experience.

32
00:02:41,328 --> 00:02:44,178
The response changes from plus one to minus one.

33
00:02:44,278 --> 00:02:49,678
We call this ability to change how the system works through experience plasticity.

34
00:02:49,778 --> 00:02:54,693
After saving and reopening, the revised relationship remains available.

35
00:02:55,783 --> 00:03:00,828
In other experiments, DEE has also used information from its environment.

36
00:03:00,903 --> 00:03:07,643
An organization can query a source, receive data, and use that information in a later
action.

37
00:03:07,828 --> 00:03:16,288
The important question is to follow the complete process: what information arrived,
what changed within the system, and what effect it produced.

38
00:03:16,363 --> 00:03:22,013
With this evidence, we can investigate how a system adapts its responses to what it
encounters.

39
00:03:23,083 --> 00:03:26,233
These advances have also been used together.

40
00:03:26,308 --> 00:03:38,068
In one experimental trajectory, DEE acquired new associations, kept earlier learning
available, and used received information to produce results.

41
00:03:38,143 --> 00:03:42,118
These capabilities were tracked throughout a single continuous history.

42
00:03:43,217 --> 00:03:52,197
Learning, remembering, revising a response, combining what has been learned, and
using information are functions we associate with intelligence.

43
00:03:52,297 --> 00:03:56,197
DEE develops mechanisms to study and connect them.

44
00:03:56,297 --> 00:04:05,022
Its cognitive value lies in the way experience can change how an organization works
and contribute to its later responses.

45
00:04:06,117 --> 00:04:09,417
These research developments come together in a platform.

46
00:04:09,492 --> 00:04:13,267
DEE Universe provides the computational universe and its rules of evolution.

47
00:04:13,472 --> 00:04:21,997
DEE thinking provides mechanisms for building organizations, running experiments,
querying results, and preserving continuity.

48
00:04:22,097 --> 00:04:27,872
DEE Cognitive brings capabilities and tools together in an application.

49
00:04:27,972 --> 00:04:34,737
This allows experimental advances to become components of increasingly functional
systems.

50
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:47,052
The technological asset is the whole: a dedicated engine, learning and memory
mechanisms, experimental tools, and an application for using them.

51
00:04:47,127 --> 00:04:55,077
This foundation supports research and the development of different solutions, with
continuity and adaptation as central capabilities.

52
00:04:56,150 --> 00:04:58,600
What could this technology be used for?

53
00:04:58,675 --> 00:05:10,557
Consider assistants that accumulate experience during use; systems that adjust their
responses when the environment changes; or research tools that help investigate how

54
00:05:10,557 --> 00:05:13,140
adaptive functions emerge and combine.

55
00:05:13,215 --> 00:05:20,350
These are development directions, with applications that need to be built and
measured against concrete problems.

56
00:05:21,417 --> 00:05:26,917
Our next goal is to turn these capabilities into verifiable applications.

57
00:05:26,967 --> 00:05:35,614
To achieve this, we seek collaboration with institutions, researchers, and companies
willing to identify a real problem, develop a pilot, and measure how the system

58
00:05:35,614 --> 00:05:38,727
responds, what it learns, and what value it generates.

59
00:05:38,802 --> 00:05:48,232
DEE is being developed in Puebla with an international vision: to explore new forms of
processing and bring research results toward technological solutions.

60
00:05:48,307 --> 00:05:50,747
DEE Cognitive 2.0.

61
00:05:50,747 --> 00:05:55,372
Learning from experience, retaining what has been learned, and building what comes
next.
